From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] sparc32: give the Solaris 2.1-2.4 boot block the OBP
 words it uses

The boot block on the CDs and disks of Solaris 2.1 to 2.4 is a small
machine-code program that hands an FCode program to "byte-load" through
the romvec's Forth interpreter (pv_fortheval). That FCode reads the UFS
file system and loads /ufsboot, using words of the OpenBoot 2.x PROMs that
it looks up by name with $find: "romvec" (with 0xffe80010, where those
PROMs keep it, if not found), "(is" to set load-base, "op-open",
"op-close", "op-read" and "op-seek" (the romvec's v2 device operations,
arguments in the C order with the first one on top), "adjust-header",
"init-program" and "?go". OpenBIOS has none of the first eight, so the
boot block printed "(is ?" and stopped with "Unhandled Exception
0x00000009" when it read the romvec at 0xffe80098. Solaris 2.5 and later
have a boot block written in C, which OpenBIOS boots.

Add the missing words to the sparc32 dictionary, make load-base a value
(as on sparc64) so that "(is" can set it, and let init-program start code
that a client has put at load-base itself: the boot block copies the ELF
segments of /ufsboot to their addresses, sets load-base to the entry
point and calls init-program and ?go. An a.out or ELF image at load-base
still goes to OpenBIOS's own init-program, with the size the client
stored in file-size.
---
 arch/sparc32/boot.c     |  9 +++++++++
 arch/sparc32/boot.h     |  1 +
 arch/sparc32/init.fs    | 44 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 arch/sparc32/openbios.c |  3 +++
 forth/admin/nvram.fs    |  5 +++++
 5 files changed, 62 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/sparc32/boot.c b/arch/sparc32/boot.c
index bb5a579..a8e3f0e 100644
--- a/arch/sparc32/boot.c
+++ b/arch/sparc32/boot.c
@@ -193,6 +193,15 @@ void setup_romvec(void)
 }
 
 
+/* init-program for code a client program has put in memory itself, starting
+   at load-base (the Solaris 2.1-2.4 boot block, see init.fs) */
+void init_program_at_load_base(void)
+{
+	feval("load-base load-state >ls.entry !");
+	arch_init_program();
+	feval("-1 state-valid !");
+}
+
 void boot(void)
 {
 	/* Boot preloaded kernel */
diff --git a/arch/sparc32/boot.h b/arch/sparc32/boot.h
index d225a31..b999c77 100644
--- a/arch/sparc32/boot.h
+++ b/arch/sparc32/boot.h
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@ int linux_load(struct sys_info *info, const char *file, const char *cmdline);
 extern const char *bootpath;
 extern void boot(void);
 extern void setup_romvec(void);
+extern void init_program_at_load_base(void);
 
 // sys_info.c
 extern unsigned int qemu_mem_size;
diff --git a/arch/sparc32/init.fs b/arch/sparc32/init.fs
index 325cc1c..fc7d40c 100644
--- a/arch/sparc32/init.fs
+++ b/arch/sparc32/init.fs
@@ -123,3 +123,47 @@ defer ignore-dfault
     " QEMU,tcx.bin" $encode-file to tcx-driver-fcode
   [THEN]
 [THEN]
+
+\ Words of the OpenBoot 2.x PROMs that the boot block of Solaris 2.1-2.4
+\ needs. That boot block is an FCode program which its machine code hands to
+\ "byte-load" through the romvec's Forth interpreter (pv_fortheval). It looks
+\ these words up by name, reads the boot device path through the romvec,
+\ loads /ufsboot from the UFS file system at load-base and starts it.
+
+\ The romvec the client programs get (set by openbios.c)
+0 value romvec
+
+\ ( x xt -- ) store x in the value or defer xt, as "to" and "is" do
+: (is ( x xt -- ) (to) ;
+
+\ The romvec's v2 device operations, arguments in the C order with the first
+\ one on top
+: op-open ( cstr -- ihandle|0 ) dup cstrlen open-dev ;
+: op-close ( ihandle -- 0 ) close-dev 0 ;
+: op-read ( len adr ihandle -- actual ) >r swap " read" r> $call-method ;
+: op-seek ( lo hi ihandle -- status ) >r " seek" r> $call-method ;
+
+\ True if load-base holds an a.out header (init-program then moves the text
+\ down over the header)
+: adjust-header ( -- aout? )
+  load-base l@ ffff and
+  dup 107 = over 108 = or over 10b = or swap 0cc = or
+;
+
+\ init-program also for a program that a client put in memory itself: an
+\ a.out or ELF image at load-base is set up as after "load" (with the size
+\ the client stored in file-size); anything else is code that starts at
+\ load-base, as OBP does. The Solaris boot block copies the ELF segments of
+\ /ufsboot to their addresses itself and then sets load-base to the entry.
+: init-program ( -- )
+  load-base l@ 7f454c46 = adjust-header or if
+    file-size @ load-state >ls.file-size !
+    init-program
+  else
+    \ bound by openbios.c
+    s" (init-program-at-load-base)" $find if execute else 2drop then
+  then
+;
+
+\ Start the program that init-program set up, if there is one
+: ?go ( -- ) state-valid @ if go then ;
diff --git a/arch/sparc32/openbios.c b/arch/sparc32/openbios.c
index 9af4e18..17d47a9 100644
--- a/arch/sparc32/openbios.c
+++ b/arch/sparc32/openbios.c
@@ -920,6 +920,8 @@ arch_init( void )
         setup_stdio();
 	/* Initialiase openprom romvec */
         romvec = init_openprom();
+	PUSH(pointer2cell(romvec));
+	feval("to romvec");
 
 	kernel_size = fw_cfg_read_i32(FW_CFG_KERNEL_SIZE);
 	if (kernel_size) {
@@ -985,6 +987,7 @@ arch_init( void )
 	
 	bind_func("platform-boot", boot );
 	bind_func("(arch-go)", setup_romvec );
+	bind_func("(init-program-at-load-base)", init_program_at_load_base );
 
 	/* Set up other properties */
         push_str("/chosen");
diff --git a/forth/admin/nvram.fs b/forth/admin/nvram.fs
index 3fbd935..7d6bf28 100644
--- a/forth/admin/nvram.fs
+++ b/forth/admin/nvram.fs
@@ -380,6 +380,11 @@ s" "         s" boot-args"            str-config    \ ???
 [IFDEF] CONFIG_SPARC64
 load-base value load-base
 [THEN]
+\ The same on sparc32, where the boot block of Solaris 2.1-2.4 sets it
+\ with "(is" (see arch/sparc32/init.fs).
+[IFDEF] CONFIG_SPARC32
+load-base value load-base
+[THEN]
 
 : release-load-area
     drop
